> API and interpretation

The four-by-four input is the exact Hadamard-basis construction from the
original report, written as explicit entries. The dense three-by-three figure
follows actual complete-row decisions; after a deflation the active row changes,
so this is not a globally monotone off-diagonal mass curve. An iteration cap is
an error budget, not an approximate-spectrum API. For the tridiagonal control,
sine eigenvectors give eigenvalues 2-2cos(j*pi/(n+1)); independent checks
compare this closed form to native results. Finite arithmetic can still overflow
and is checked. Default order256,1000 steps per block and history1,000,000
entries are configurable.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

